    {
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 1 },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "content": "> ⚠️ **Domain Boundary Notice: Layer 4/7 Transport vs Media & Telephony Health**\n>\n> A successful TCP 3-way handshake or TLS session negotiation to Avaya SBCE port 5061 (`endpoint.service.reachable = 1`) proves **only** that socket connectivity exists across the network perimeter.\n>\n> It does **NOT** verify:\n> 1. SIP User Agent Digest Authentication or SIP Registration state.\n> 2. SDP offer/answer codec negotiation (e.g. G.711 A-law / G.729).\n> 3. NAT traversal or asymmetric media routing (e.g. one-way RTP audio).\n> 4. End-to-end voice quality (ITU-T G.107 MOS) or packet jitter.\n>\n> Comprehensive voice service assurance correlates **both** endpoint edge reachability and controlled synthetic Asterisk call probes.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.6.0",
      "title": "Voice Observability Domain Boundary",
      "type": "text"
    },
